## 6. `include/strata/core/conversation_cache.hpp` — Parked Conversation Policy

**Responsibilities:** Manages a bounded LRU cache of `SavedConversation` entries with byte budget and slot limits, prefix matching over token IDs and image keys, K/V reuse retention, and eviction accounting.

**Proposed change:** Add a `touch(size_t index)` method that moves an entry to the back of the deque (most-recently-used) without copying its data, so a cache hit updates recency without a full move.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/core/conversation_cache.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/core/conversation_cache.hpp
@@ -118,6 +118,14 @@
     SavedConversation take(size_t index) {
         SavedConversation out = std::move(entries_.at(index));
         bytes_ -= out.bytes();
         entries_.erase(entries_.begin() + (std::ptrdiff_t) index);
         return out;
     }
+    /// Move entry `index` to the back (most recently used) without copying its payload.
+    void touch(size_t index) {
+        if (index == entries_.size() - 1) return;
+        auto it = entries_.begin() + (std::ptrdiff_t) index;
+        std::rotate(it, it + 1, entries_.end());
+    }

     // Reserve before allocating a snapshot. held is an incoming image removed
```

**Verification cases:**
1. Insert 3 conversations (A, B, C), call `touch(0)`; confirm the deque order is B, C, A and `best()` still finds A at index 2.
2. Call `touch(entries_.size()-1)` on the last entry; confirm no rotation occurs and the order is unchanged.

